---
// THE ILL-TEMPERED WEEK — a week of the web's attention, composed (2026-11-09; method:
// docs/design/2026-11-08-common-time-method.md). The music first, then what each piece hears, then how it is
// made. The page plays the newest complete album in full and, while a week runs, that week's Overlooked as far as
// it has grown. Every number on the page is read at build time from the albums' own records
// (src/data/ill-tempered-week/<week>.json), which the renderer wrote beside the audio; the guard
// (src/lib/ill-tempered-week/albums.test.ts) holds each record to the day files it names.
import SheetHead from '@/components/experiments/SheetHead.astro'
import SheetFoot from '@/components/experiments/SheetFoot.astro'
import OverlookedDays from '@/components/ill-tempered-week/OverlookedDays.astro'
import { clock, readAlbums, span, weekday } from '@/lib/ill-tempered-week/albums'
import '@/styles/experiment-sheet.css'
import '@/styles/ill-tempered-week.css'

const REPO = 'https://github.com/frankbueltge/frankbueltge.de'
const link = 'underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-fg'
const pct = (x: number): string => `${Math.round(100 * x)} %`

const albums = readAlbums()
const newest = albums.at(-1)!
// The album the page plays in full: the newest complete one (the growing week, only until one exists).
const album = albums.filter((a) => a.complete).at(-1) ?? newest
// The week that is still growing, shown above the album while it runs.
const growing = newest.complete || newest === album ? null : newest
const earlier = albums.filter((a) => a !== album && a !== growing).reverse()
const o = album.pieces.overlooked
const u = album.pieces.unison
const t = album.pieces.turn
const g = growing?.pieces.overlooked
const recordHref = (week: string): string => `${REPO}/blob/main/src/data/ill-tempered-week/${week}.json`
const turnDay = t?.days.find((d) => d.turn)
const peaks = u ? u.days.filter((d) => d.peak) : []
const most = u ? u.days.reduce((a, b) => (b.agreement > a.agreement ? b : a)) : null
const badges = growing && g
  ? [`${album.title}, complete`, `${growing.title}, edition ${g.edition} of 7`]
  : [album.title, album.complete ? 'complete' : `edition ${o.edition} of 7`]
---

<main id="main" class="sheet mx-auto w-full max-w-5xl flex-1 px-4 py-10 sm:py-14">
  <SheetHead
    kicker="From the nightly-ledger line"
    title="The Ill-Tempered Week"
    sub="A week of the web’s attention, composed. Each week is an album, a Contrapunctus numbered by the week, pressed day by day from Common Ground: what was overlooked, where the press agreed, when the week turned."
    badges={badges}
    stamp={span(album.days)}
  />

  <section class="mb-12 max-w-3xl" aria-label="About the album">
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      Three pieces in three idioms: a chamber ensemble, a string orchestra with brass and timpani, and electronics. Real
      instruments, recorded notes tuned to just intonation on A; synthetic voices that say what the week said. No music model is
      involved: every note follows a written rule from a committed day file, and the album’s record names each file it read. While
      the week runs, <em>Overlooked</em> is pressed again from the days so far each time a day of the ledger lands, so the piece grows and ends on the
      newest day; when the week is complete, <em>Unison</em> and <em>Turn</em> join it and the album is never pressed again.
    </p>
  </section>

  {growing && g && (
    <section class="itw-piece itw-growing mb-14" aria-label="This week so far">
      <p class="kicker mb-1">This week · {growing.title} · {span(growing.days)}</p>
      <h2 class="itw-title">Overlooked, so far</h2>
      <audio class="itw-player mt-3" controls preload="metadata" src={g.audio}></audio>
      <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-mono-sm text-fg-muted">
        {clock(g.seconds)} · edition {g.edition} of 7, to {weekday(g.newest_day)} ·
        <a class={link} href={g.audio} download>download</a> · CC BY 4.0
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        The running week, pressed from its days so far. Each new day of the ledger adds a day, and the piece is pressed again from the start,
        so this edition breaks off at its newest day and the next one hears the week differently: a motif ends with its
        day once a later day no longer names its field. Once Sunday’s day is in, the piece is complete, and <em>Unison</em> and
        <em>Turn</em> join it.
      </p>
      <OverlookedDays piece={g} />
    </section>
  )}

  {growing && <p class="kicker mb-6">The album · {album.title} · {span(album.days)}</p>}

  <section class="itw-piece mb-14" aria-label="Overlooked">
    <p class="kicker mb-1">I · chamber ensemble</p>
    <h2 class="itw-title">Overlooked</h2>
    <audio class="itw-player mt-3" controls preload="metadata" src={o.audio}></audio>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-mono-sm text-fg-muted">
      {clock(o.seconds)} · {album.complete ? 'seven days' : `edition ${o.edition} of 7, to ${weekday(o.newest_day)}`} ·
      <a class={link} href={o.audio} download>download</a> · CC BY 4.0
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
      Each day, the headline that drew the least attention on its own platform, among all thirteen fields of the map and from a
      field not heard before that week, is said once. The instrument of its field answers with the headline’s own speech melody,
      in the rhythm it was spoken; then the melody becomes a motif, and violins, violas, piano, cellos and basses take it up in
      canon. Earlier days keep sounding, softer by the day, so the overlooked gather into a polyphony across the week, while the
      day’s most attended headlines murmur underneath and give way. A day’s motif ends with its day if the newest day no longer
      names its field.
    </p>
    <OverlookedDays piece={o} />
  </section>

  {u && most && (
    <section class="itw-piece mb-14" aria-label="Unison">
      <p class="kicker mb-1">II · string orchestra, brass, timpani</p>
      <h2 class="itw-title">Unison</h2>
      <audio class="itw-player mt-3" controls preload="metadata" src={u.audio}></audio>
      <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-mono-sm text-fg-muted">
        {clock(u.seconds)} · war and violence · <a class={link} href={u.audio} download>download</a> · CC BY 4.0
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        Every signal that named war and violence is one string glissando: its section by the attention it drew on its platform,
        the most attended highest, its first pitch from its own headline as spoken, its entry at the hour it was published. Each
        day the whole mass glides towards A’s harmonic chord exactly as far as the press agreed: the share of the day’s war
        signals naming its most named story. Where the press agreed, brass and timpani take up the chord and the day’s most attended
        headline is said over it; after each peak a solo double bass plays the speech melody of the day’s least attended war
        headline, outside the chord. The press agreed most on {weekday(most.day)}, {pct(most.agreement)} on {most.story};
        {peaks.length === u.days.length ? ' every day reached the chord.' : ` ${u.days.length - peaks.length} of ${u.days.length} days stayed a cluster.`}
      </p>
      <ol class="itw-agree mt-5" aria-label="Agreement by day">
        {u.days.map((d) => (
          <li>
            <span class="font-mono text-mono-sm text-fg-muted">{weekday(d.day).slice(0, 3)}</span>
            <svg class="itw-bar" viewBox="0 0 100 6" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect class="itw-track" x="0" y="0" width="100" height="6"></rect>
              <rect class={d.peak ? 'itw-fill' : 'itw-fill itw-none'} x="0" y="0" width={Math.round(100 * d.agreement)} height="6"></rect>
            </svg>
            <span class="font-mono text-mono-sm">{pct(d.agreement)} {d.story}{d.peak ? '' : ' · no chord'}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>
  )}

  {t && (
    <section class="itw-piece mb-14" aria-label="Turn">
      <p class="kicker mb-1">III · electronics</p>
      <h2 class="itw-title">Turn</h2>
      <audio class="itw-player mt-3" controls preload="metadata" src={t.audio}></audio>
      <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-mono-sm text-fg-muted">
        {clock(t.seconds)} · AI and its harms · <a class={link} href={t.audio} download>download</a> · CC BY 4.0
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        A rhythmicon of the platform families: each pulses as many beats a bar as its harmonic number (search 5, news 6, social 7,
        tech 9) and sings its vowel on that harmonic of A; how many of its beats sound is its count of AI signals that day, so the
        bar fills as attention does. Busy days run faster. {turnDay
          ? <>The week turned on {weekday(turnDay.day)}, with {turnDay.signals} signals: one bar sounds every beat of every family, and a silent bar carries the day’s most attended AI headline, “{turnDay.said}”.</>
          : <>This week did not turn.</>}
      </p>
    </section>
  )}

  <section class="mb-12 max-w-3xl" aria-label="How it is made">
    <p class="kicker mb-3">How it is made</p>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      The counts are the house’s one count over Common Ground’s day files, the fields those of the map; a headline’s attention is
      its place among the signals of its own platform that day (Hacker News points, Bluesky posts, Trends searches, Polymarket
      dollars, Wikipedia views, Google News editions). Instruments: {album.library}. Voices: {album.voices}. Each album’s record
      hashes every day file it read: <a class={link} href={recordHref(album.week)}>{album.title}</a>{growing && <>, <a class={link} href={recordHref(growing.week)}>{growing.title}</a></>}.
    </p>
  </section>

  {earlier.length > 0 && (
    <section class="mb-12" aria-label="Earlier albums">
      <p class="kicker mb-3">Earlier albums</p>
      <ul class="itw-albums">
        {earlier.map((a) => (
          <li>
            <p class="font-mono text-mono-sm text-fg-muted">
              {a.title} · {span(a.days)} · <a class={link} href={recordHref(a.week)}>record</a>
            </p>
            {Object.entries(a.pieces).map(([name, p]) => (
              <p class="mt-1"><span class="font-mono text-mono-sm">{name}</span> <audio class="itw-player mt-1" controls preload="none" src={p!.audio}></audio></p>
            ))}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>
  )}

  <SheetFoot links={[
    { href: '/werke/ill-tempered-week', label: 'method sheet' },
    { href: `${REPO}/tree/main/src/data/ill-tempered-week`, label: 'the records', external: true },
    { href: `${REPO}/tree/main/scripts/ill-tempered-week`, label: 'the renderer', external: true },
    { href: '/trending', label: 'Common Ground' },
  ]} />
</main>
